  "label": "User projected onto the textual slogan 'my body my choice'",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the text 'my body my choice' overlaid on the image. This projection implies that the user is identifying with or adopting the slogan as their own stance, even though the visual metaphor of erasing 'Abortion' directly contradicts the pro-choice message. The projection is implicit, not explicit, but the slogan's placement and the meme's overall intent create a framing where the viewer is invited to see themselves as the holder of the 'my body my choice' principle, despite the visual act of erasure.",
